.\" asa.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX asa(1) utility, which this
.\" tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/ASA.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/ASA.
.TH ASA 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
asa \- interpret carriage-control characters
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Asa
is not provided on maux.
no Fortran carriage-control convention is used or supported on
this machine.
